## Argument for Matlab against COMSOL

While high-fidelity multiphysics simulations (e.g. COMSOL) provide a 
detailed representation of coupled flow and heat transfer processes, 
their computational cost limits their applicability for long-term and 
parametric studies. Reduced-order models, such as the one developed in 
this work, enable efficient simulations while retaining control over 
individual physical mechanisms. This allows for a systematic investigation 
of modeling assumptions, such as the representation of buoyancy-driven 
mixing, and helps to identify the limitations of one-dimensional approaches.